{
  "name": "high_output_heart_failure",
  "remarks": [
    "Simulates high-output heart failure in adults with risk factors: anemia or pregnancy.",
    "Hyperthyroidism and AV fistula are also clinically recognized risk factors but are not",
    "modelled here -- no module in this tree sets either attribute, so both were dead guard",
    "arms (see CheckRiskFactors) until removed 2026-08. Modelling them for real would need new",
    "hyperthyroidism/AV-fistula onset logic elsewhere in the tree, out of this task's scope.",
    "Every encounter is closed by an EncounterEnd before any delay or loop: this module otherwise holds the engine's per-person encounter reservation for life, which blocks wellness visits and every other module's encounters."
  ],
  "states": {
    "Initial": {
      "type": "Initial",
      "direct_transition": "CheckRiskFactors"
    },
    "CheckRiskFactors": {
      "type": "Guard",
      "allow": {
        "condition_type": "And",
        "conditions": [
          {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": ">=",
            "quantity": 20,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": "<=",
            "quantity": 70,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          {
            "condition_type": "Or",
            "remarks": [
              "Dropped two arms that were permanently dead: `hyperthyroidism` and `av_fistula` are",
              "both real clinical risk factors for high-output HF, but neither attribute is set by",
              "any module in this tree (`grep -rl \"hyperthyroidism\\|av_fistula\" src/main/resources/modules/`",
              "returns only this file), so both conditions could only ever evaluate false. Deleted",
              "rather than wired to a setter -- this module models `anemia` and `pregnant` (both are",
              "genuinely set elsewhere in the tree) as its risk-factor population; adding real",
              "hyperthyroidism/AV-fistula modelling is out of this task's scope."
            ],
            "conditions": [
              {
                "condition_type": "Attribute",
                "attribute": "anemia",
                "operator": "is not nil"
              },
              {
                "condition_type": "Attribute",
                "attribute": "pregnant",
                "operator": "==",
                "value": true
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "direct_transition": "HighOutputHF_Incidence_Gate"
    },
    "OnsetHighOutputHF": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "CROSS-MODULE GATE (audit Class 7, task 5.2 group 4) -- the heart-failure",
        "quartet. Four top-level modules each diagnose their own heart-failure code",
        "with no coordination, so one patient could carry all four at once and run",
        "four competing maintenance/decompensation loops against them:",
        "  congestive_heart_failure.json   88805009 Chronic congestive heart failure",
        "  high_output_heart_failure.json  10091002 High output heart failure",
        "  right_sided_heart_failure.json  10335000 Chronic right sided heart failure",
        "  valvular_heart_failure.json     42343007 Congestive heart failure",
        "Rule: FIRST-TO-DIAGNOSE WINS. Each module tests the other three codes on its",
        "own onset path; whichever module gets there first owns the patient's heart",
        "failure and the other three stand down.",
        "Only the primary code of each rival is tested. That is not a shortcut: the",
        "record key is codes[0] (HealthRecord.conditionStart keys `present` by",
        "primaryCode), so high_output_heart_failure.json's secondary ICD-10 entries",
        "I50.9 / I50.89 never enter `present` and cannot be matched by an Active",
        "Condition check. No module in the tree emits a ConditionEnd for any of these",
        "four codes (verified by grep), so once one is set the other three modules'",
        "checks stay true for life.",
        "",
        "This is the EARLY gate. It sits before the cardiology encounter opens, so a",
        "patient who already has a heart-failure diagnosis from a rival module never",
        "gets this module's workup visit, its echo/BNP/imaging or its drug orders. No",
        "encounter is open at this point, so Terminal leaks no encounter lock.",
        "It is not sufficient on its own: State$Encounter.process returns false --",
        "blocks across ticks -- while another module holds this person's encounter",
        "lock, so the verdict here can go stale. The recheck below re-tests once the",
        "encounter has actually opened."
      ],
      "conditional_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Active Condition",
            "codes": [
              {
                "system": "SNOMED-CT",
                "code": "88805009",
                "display": "Chronic congestive heart failure (disorder)"
              },
              {
                "system": "SNOMED-CT",
                "code": "10335000",
                "display": "Chronic right sided heart failure"
              },
              {
                "system": "SNOMED-CT",
                "code": "42343007",
                "display": "Congestive heart failure"
              }
            ]
          },
          "transition": "Terminal"
        },
        {
          "transition": "OnsetHighOutputHF_Action_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "HighOutputHF_Maintenance": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "range": {
        "low": 30,
        "high": 90,
        "unit": "days"
      },
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.1,
          "transition": "HighOutputHF_Decompensation"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.9,
          "transition": "HighOutputHF_Maintenance_Actions"
        }
      ]
    },
