    "HighOutputHF_Incidence_Gate": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "High-output heart failure is rare even among patients with the risk factors above;",
        "without this gate the Guard admits the majority of the population.",
        "",
        "Calibration target: high-output HF should be <=2% of all heart failure. Sources:",
        "- Reddy YNV, Melenovsky V, Redfield MM, Nishimura RA, Borlaug BA. High-Output Heart",
        "  Failure: A 15-Year Experience. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2016;68(5):473-482 -- of patients",
        "  referred for right-heart catheterization (already cardiac-symptomatic), only ~0.7%",
        "  had definite high-output HF.",
        "- Heart Failure Society of America, HF Stats 2024 -- ~6.7 million US adults (20+) live",
        "  with heart failure, ~1.9-2.8% (~2.3% midpoint) prevalence of the adult population.",
        "  A <=2% HOHF share of that implies HOHF should be roughly <=0.05% of all adults.",
        "",
        "This gate previously fired at 0.02 (2%) against the CheckRiskFactors-gated population",
        "(anyone aged 20-70 who is ever anemic or pregnant) -- a materially larger and healthier",
        "population than Reddy et al.'s cardiac-catheterization-referred cohort, so 2% here",
        "overshoots the <=2%-of-all-HF target by a wide margin once anemia/pregnancy prevalence",
        "in that gate population is accounted for. Lowered by 10x to 0.002 (0.2%), below even",
        "Reddy et al.'s 0.7% figure for a sicker, pre-selected population -- reasonable given this",
        "module's Guard only requires anemia or pregnancy, not any existing cardiac symptoms.",
        "Honest caveat: the exact population-level HOHF share of all-HF output depends on this",
        "tree's other HF modules and on anemia/pregnancy prevalence in the simulated population,",
        "neither of which this task's scope allows verifying empirically (no smoke/generation",
        "runs). 0.002 is a literature-anchored, order-of-magnitude-correct reduction, not a",
        "smoke-verified final calibration -- flagging for empirical re-check once a run is available."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "transition": "OnsetHighOutputHF",
          "distribution": 0.002
        },
        {
          "transition": "Terminal",
          "distribution": 0.998
        }
      ]
    },
